WEBVTT

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.330
Just our luck! Sheesh!

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:13.960
Grrrrrrrrrrrrr!

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.340
Grah, this is taking forever!

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.080
Quit acting so antsy!

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.680
Shuddup! You’re the one 
with ants in yer pants!

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.840
Excuse me?!

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:27.840
It’s here!

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.560
No!

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.900
Huh? What?! I’d like to 
cancel this cancellation!

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.020
What’s up, Nonoha?

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.470
Ana and Cube said 
they’d meet us there.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.760
Hey, they for reals?

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:44.820
It’s all cool.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:45.730
Why?

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.730
I am the Giver.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.570
You are the Solver.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.540
And the prize is...

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.740
Jin Makata.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.830
Let’s solve it together!

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.490
We’ll solve this massive

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:59.410
puzzle Raetsel made that 
uses the world as its stage!

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.270
It was cancelled?

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.620
I see. Very well.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.450
Mr. President.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.510
Shall I change your plans?

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.190
Unanticipated events can 
also pose as opportunities.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:57.030
Just Now, I Was Thinking of Someone

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.920
This is bigger than Kegon Falls!

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:14.920
This feels heavenly!

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.170
Ana!

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.350
Stop that! Don’t lean over the edge!

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.400
Do you realize what would 
happen if you fell?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.180
I, Ana, think that 
waterfalls are wonderful!

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.940
The spray of water feels so good!

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:27.780
Geez!

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.320
I wanna get wet!

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.320
I hope Kaito and the 
others get here soon.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:35.080
Splitter splatter! Splitter 
splatter! Splitter splatter!

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:35.080
Once I’ve joined the party, 
Raetsel’s challenge will be as good as solved.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.200
<i>Evading danger! Evading danger!</i>

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:40.210
<i>Evading danger! Evading danger!</i>

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.580
<i>Evading danger!</i>

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.670
Iwarin, you look hip in that raincoat!

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.050
<i>The doctor bought it for me.</i>

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:48.840
<i>The doctor bought it for me.</i>

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.580
But it isn’t raining...

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:54.280
He’s been demanding 
ever since I increased

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.030
his autonomous learning capacity.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.870
<i>Must be wary of water from the falls.</i>

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.140
<i>May get wet!</i>

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.400
He’s built to handle land and water!

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.400
<i>Must be wary of water from the falls.</i>

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.230
<i> May get wet!</i>

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.190
I just got a text from Nonoha.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.660
They’re having such bad weather 
that the plane can’t takeoff.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.600
Then let’s go sightseeing!

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.490
This feels great!

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.490
Whoa!

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.980
Jeez, Ana! That’s dangerous!

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.980
This feels great!

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:20.360
<i>Danger! Danger!</i>

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.250
<i>Every minute, 3.6 billion liters 
of water gush over the waterfalls.</i>

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:27.640
<i>Calculating the daily amount of water</i>

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.760
<i>that splashes on a tourist 
boat built to hold twenty.</i>

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.740
<i>Calculating... Calculating...</i>

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:36.880
Aw, jeez! Forget about the waterfalls!

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.440
There is plenty of work

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.230
we can do on our own 
before Kaito arrives!

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.380
Rainbows!

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.940
I think they’re rainbows!

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.240
You’re right. They’re rainbows...

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.020
Those are Naipi’s rainbows.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.520
There is a legend behind those rainbows.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.290
Naipi is the name of a beautiful lady

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.780
who was supposed to be offered to 
the god that resides in this river.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.550
Yeah?

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.800
Are you here to see the sights?

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:11.880
Yup!

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.740
“Yup,” is the wrong answer!

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.910
We’re meeting up 
with our friends here.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:19.240
In that case, what do you say

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.550
I give you a mini-tour 
until your friends arrive?

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.440
But we have our own agenda--

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.150
Yay! Splish-splash waterfall fun!

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:27.860
Ana!

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.610
<i>Danger! Danger!</i>

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.610
Waterfall splash! Super refreshing!

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:33.900
Rainbow! They can’t 
say a thing! O Rainbow!

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.900
Iwashimizu, forget about 
the waterfalls! Rainbow!

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.690
I’m Regina. It’s a 
pleasure to meet you.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.370
I’m Ana! He’s Q-taro!

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:40.870
I’m Cubik!

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.080
And he’s Iwashimizu.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.940
<i>Danger! Danger!</i>

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:48.040
Quit going on about the 
waterfalls already!

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:56.680
Long, long ago, the people 
who lived by the riverbank

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:00.420
feared the power of the 
serpent god, M’boi.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.790
So every year, they 
offered him a sacrifice

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.340
in the form of a beautiful maiden.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:09.220
Naipi was one of the ladies chosen 
to serve as a human sacrifice.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:15.450
And she was also the first woman 
who dared to defy M’boi.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.350
If you’re wondering why, 
it’s because she had a lover.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.540
M’boi was furious when 
he learned that Naipi was

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.110
trying to flee with her beloved.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:35.230
In his rage, he split the river apart.

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:40.000
It’s said that is how 
Iguazu Falls came to be.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.210
M’boi’s rage would not subside

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:46.170
even as the canoe was being 
devoured by the waterfall.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.570
He would not grant the 
lovers one last moment

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.390
of happiness by allowing 
them to die together.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:58.740
M’boi transformed Naipi into the 
rock in the basin of the falls.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.530
Her lover was turned into a palm tree.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:03.330
And he kept a close eye on the two.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.080
Poor Naipi...

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.530
Men green with jealousy 
sure can be scary!

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.880
But remember those rainbows?

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:14.340
A good god took pity on Naipi...

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.440
And on clear days,

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:19.540
he creates rainbows to connect 
the rock and the palm trees.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:24.490
The rainbow is able to carry 
Naipi’s burning love

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:26.540
to her special someone.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:28.840
Or so we assume...

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:33.120
I, Ana, think you’re like Naipi.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:37.400
Just now, you were thinking of someone.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:45.190
Boo-yah! I freed it!

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:47.540
This one’s next!

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:50.080
I’m on fire!

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.500
I swear, all you ever 
do is play puzzles!

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.420
I’m amazed you don’t 
get sick of them.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.960
Yeah and you keep stuffing your face!

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:58.170
Can you blame me

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:01.140
when we’re gonna be stuck 
here for who knows how long?

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:05.580
Maybe I should conquer all of 
the restaurants on this floor!

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.730
I’ll stand my own via 
nam pla! Er, number games!

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:09.780
Say what?!

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:22.320
Aren’t the butterflies pretty?

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:27.150
Ana, we aren’t here 
to look at butterflies!

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:30.650
You two came to find 
someone, didn’t you?

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.880
That sounds about right.

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:35.170
We’re looking for these two.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:36.780
Have you seen them?

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.790
I’m not sure...

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.510
May I borrow these photos?

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.040
I’ll ask my friends 
if they’ve seen them.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:48.790
Thank you, Ms. Regina!

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:05.190
Hello?

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:06.480
Ana?

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.560
Oh, Regi-Regi!

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:12.000
One of my friends said she spotted them.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.380
The people you’re 
searching for, I mean.

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:16.690
Rae-Rae and Jin-Jin?

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:18.910
Right. Those are the two.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:21.340
Let’s go check it out tomorrow.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:24.390
No, I don’t mind.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:26.920
Well, sweet dreams!

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:36.520
President Enigma, I swear 
by my name, Regina,

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:39.480
that I will annihilate 
those vile puzzlers.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:56.500
<i>Divine! Divine! Divine! Divine!</i>

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:07.470
I, Ana, think this is 
thrilling to the max!

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:09.350
I hate boats!

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.520
Ugh, I feel sick!

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:16.060
The place where she saw your 
friends is just up ahead!

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:20.510
Just up ahead?!

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:23.570
You can’t be serious!

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:31.370
Where are we?

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:34.290
I didn’t realize there was 
a cave behind the waterfalls.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:37.370
We’ll have to take a 
canoe the rest of the way.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.970
The canoe goes swish swash!

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:49.790
This place gives me the creeps!

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:05.090
Is this a...

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:06.680
Could this be a...

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:08.990
puzzle?!

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:15.380
Regi-Regi!

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:19.020
I’m not simply Regina.

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:22.450
I am President Enigma’s 
Third Secretary,

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:27.340
the Master Brain, Regina Maria Vasco!

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:31.800
I have plans here today.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:35.640
They are to defeat the two of 
you with this Puzzle of Fools.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:36.540
That is all!

00:11:37.390 --> 00:11:40.600
Regi-Regi, you aren’t Naipi anymore...

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.690
You thought I was Naipi?

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.650
You are quite the comedian!

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:48.630
You’re talking to the woman who

00:11:48.630 --> 00:11:50.080
once abandoned her boyfriend

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:53.740
to work under President 
Enigma as his secretary.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:57.510
In my eyes, the President 
is none other than

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.780
Iguazu’s serpent god, 
M’boi, in human skin!

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:04.300
I don’t care to be compared to Naipi,

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.590
who failed to see the value 
behind such a glorious god.

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:11.470
Now risk your lives as you 
face this Puzzle of Fools!

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:15.890
Then you will come to realize just 
how glorious the President is!

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:20.170
I’ve gotta try my hardest for Kaito...

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:23.290
Allow me to explain the rules.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.750
You will travel on that canoe 
while indicating how much water

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:29.310
gets moved via a control panel.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:32.650
If all of the pools contain equal

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:35.620
quantities of water by the 
time you reach the goal,

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.640
I will declare you victorious.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:43.150
You have twenty minutes.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:45.880
If you exceed that time limit...

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:50.280
Much like what you just witnessed,

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:51.930
the bottom of all of those 
pools will fall off.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.570
You will share the same 
fate as the canoe

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:55.220
that gets flushed down with the water.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:59.350
Thus President Enigma’s 
wish to see the

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:01.980
annihilation of you Phi-Brain children

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.300
will finally be realized!

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:08.980
Kaito mentioned “Raetsel’s 
puzzle.” Is this part of it?

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:13.610
Indeed, it is! Naturally, 
I have prepared a prize.

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.620
What should we do, Q-taro?

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:21.400
There are a total of 38 
portions of water spread

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.320
across all of the pools.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:27.070
If I divided that across the 16 pools...

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:33.080
there wouldn’t be enough 
water to use three portions.

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:36.570
So to disperse it uniformly, it’d 
take zero, one or two portions...

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:40.630
Now then, start the puzzle!

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:47.770
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:53.610
Looking at this, the two pools by the 
goal are already three-fourths full.

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:57.050
In which case, they’ll both have

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:00.040
four portions of water 
when more floods in.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:04.160
To equally distribute their 
four portions across the goal,

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.030
I must divide four by 
two, which equals two.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:10.450
I’d like to fill all of the 
pools with two portions, but...

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:10.240
Q-taro! Q-taro!

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:13.970
If I did that, I’d have 
six portions leftover.

00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:19.010
Q-taro! Q-taro!

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:21.220
Why don’t we spill some?

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:23.890
Splash!

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:25.380
That’s it!

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:27.970
We just need to spill 
out the excess water.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:32.640
In which case, our 
path to the goal is...

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:46.120
Next we’re going to Pool F!

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.260
Sweet! Next up is Pool B!

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:06.890
Is she emptying all of 
the water out of Pool G?

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:09.360
Pool G already contained two portions,

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:11.260
so I didn’t include it in my course.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.850
Now we have to start over!

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:19.950
In order to win, anything is fair game.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:23.110
<i>That is one of the rules 
we Master Brains abide by.</i>

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:28.110
<i>Searching for the doctor. 
Searching for the doctor.</i>

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:32.880
<i>Searching for the doctor. 
Searching for the doctor.</i>

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:37.550
<i>Searching for the doctor. 
Searching for the doctor.</i>

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:41.390
If we have to go through Pool G,

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:44.130
we’ll have to pass 
through all of the pools.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:48.890
In that case, we’re stuck passing 
through one of the pools twice.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:52.520
We’ll have to backtrack 
through F or K...

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:56.780
And since Regina removed two 
portions of water from Pool G,

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:59.140
that will leave us with three 
portions of excess water.

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:00.770
In that case...!

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:19.300
Ana, watch it!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:23.540
Row, row! Row, row! Row, row! 
Row, row! Row, row! Row, row!

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:28.520
<i>Searching for the doctor. 
Searching for the doctor.</i>

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:31.050
<i>Power Search, commence!</i>

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:34.860
<i>Search, complete!</i>

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:38.520
<i>Doctor!</i>

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:54.950
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave!

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:07.790
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:31.730
I wonder if Naipi and her 
boyfriend felt like this

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:33.860
when M’boi attacked them.

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:36.240
Are Ana and Q-taro lovers?!

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:38.490
That’s not what I meant!

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.000
Why don’t you join me?

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:57.010
I am the President of the Republic 
of Amgine, Johan Sigmund Enigma.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.120
The President...?

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:04.560
You are overflowing 
with talent as a Giver.

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:09.190
I’m... overflowing with talent?

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:23.300
If I don’t give results...

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:28.350
I’ll never become President 
Enigma’s personal secretary!

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:41.740
Next up is the goal!

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:51.370
May President Enigma be victorious!

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.170
Waterfall splash?!

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:01.210
I’ll do whatever it takes to win.

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:04.910
Please watch me, President Enigma!

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:12.290
We’re short one portion!

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:19.480
Time is almost up.

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:23.180
Once the timer hits zero, the bottom 
of those pools will pop off!

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:26.680
<i>The doctor’s in a pinch!
 The doctor’s in a pinch!</i>

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:31.940
<i>Calculating. Calculating.</i>

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.750
<i>Calculating. Calculating.</i>

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:38.330
<i>Calculating. Calculating.</i>

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:39.820
<i>Complete!</i>

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:42.810
<i>Doctor!</i>

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:46.330
<i>Doctor!</i>

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:48.220
<i>Iwashimizu!</i>

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:49.470
Iwarin!

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:52.140
<i>Doctor!</i>

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:56.850
<i>After this, it has a 
100% chance of falling.</i>

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:22.080
The stony icicle worked as 
a substitute for the water.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.490
We owe you, Iwashimizu!

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:32.920
“In order to win, 
anything is fair game.”

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:37.230
Don’t you love that saying, Ma’am?

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:44.320
Th-the First Secretary?

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:45.760
Hello?

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:48.820
What?! I’m fired?!

00:20:49.190 --> 00:20:51.160
Please give me just one more chance!

00:20:56.370 --> 00:21:00.400
Miss, do you think you could hand 
over that prize you promised us?

00:21:21.850 --> 00:21:24.170
Iwashimizu, answer the door!

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:26.180
<i>Roger! Roger!</i>

00:21:27.020 --> 00:21:28.680
<i>Who’s there? Who’s there?</i>

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:32.490
Hey, Cube! Ana!

00:21:32.990 --> 00:21:34.180
Sorry to have kept ya waitin’!

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:38.240
Together, you make the 
AnaQ-maki sushi roll!

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:40.690
Let’s go hit Raetsel’s next puzzle!

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:45.630
What’s wrong with you two?

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:47.450
Here.

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:51.300
What’s that?

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:53.200
This is--!

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:56.080
<i>Mission complete! Mission complete!</i>

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:58.060
What’s goin’ on here?

00:21:58.060 --> 00:21:59.350
Beats me.

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:02.180
Hey, Cubik!

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:03.640
Ana! Wake up! C’mon!

00:22:03.640 --> 00:22:07.080
Give us an explanation! I mean it!

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:07.820
Whoa! You shouldn’t shake 
them around like that!

00:22:18.240 --> 00:22:19.910
Worthless.

00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:24.990
Those Master Brains 
were truly worthless.

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:28.340
It would appear that my turn has come.

00:24:02.600 --> 00:24:04.640
Greetings! I have not seen 
you in quite some time.

00:24:04.640 --> 00:24:05.840
I am Herbert.

00:24:06.230 --> 00:24:09.730
I shall invite the ultimate Solver, 
Kaito Daimon, over for our next episode.

00:24:09.730 --> 00:24:12.690
We will have fun discussing 
current events and puzzles.

00:24:12.690 --> 00:24:13.980
There will also be an alpaca.

00:24:13.980 --> 00:24:15.510
I hope you look forward to the episode!

00:24:15.730 --> 00:24:18.150
Next time, “Is That What 
You Thought I’d Say?”

00:24:16.490 --> 00:24:27.980
Is That What You Thought I’d Say?

00:24:18.150 --> 00:24:20.160
Of course that’s not 
what the episode is about!

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:21.870
Prepare yourself, Kaito Daimon!

00:24:21.870 --> 00:24:26.900
You will pay for your heinous act of 
insulting me by suffering disgrace and despair!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
